Fig. 6. Human-centered Design Process [ISO 9241-210:2019] As defined in International Organization for Standardization (ISO) standard 9241-210:2019 [248], HCD involves:

• an explicit understanding of users, tasks and environments–the context of use;

• the involvement of users throughout design and development;

• a design driven and refined by human-centered evaluation;

• an iterative process whereby a prototype is designed, tested and modified;

• addressing the whole user experience;

• a design team including multidisciplinary skills and perspectives. Based on the ISO standard, a HCD methodology for the development of AI systems could iteratively comprise the following, as shown in Fig. 7:

